  "why": "The statement asks about arbitrary j: V→V without AC. Kunen and Zapletal use AC, so they are variants. Suzuki settles the case of j definable from parameters in ZF, a refereed pre-snapshot case. Schlutzenberg (V_λ+2), Jeon (cofinal j, no Powerset, possibly a well-ordered base), the Wholeness/BTEE theories and Mohammed (a ZFC(j) proof) each change the question, so they are variants. The two McCallum preprints would have refuted the V→V form by restriction, so their scope is whole, but both were withdrawn by the author for named errors, so both are knocked_down. Goldberg's conditional results, the talk abstracts and the adjacent papers settle nothing. On the UQ answers: AI models produced the text, but it concerns a neighbouring question, nobody checked it, and the answers contradict each other. It is discarded as a variant, so I set the AI role to none rather than credit unchecked output as generated mathematics.",
